course: dictionary
lesson: 8749
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have many meanings, and the words around it show you which one is meant. «A loaf has a set number of slices» means fixed, decided in advance. In «Set the cups on the table», set means to put something somewhere. Same spelling, different jobs.
explain: Ask what word would fit in the place of set. Then try your meaning in the sentence. In «A shift is a set time at work», a set time is a fixed time, so the shift starts and ends at the same time each day. If your meaning makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
explain: Some words tell you what kind of word they are. In «A set of six cups», the set is a group of things. In «Set the table», you are doing something, so set is a verb. Look for a thing, an action, or a description, and you will know which meaning to choose.
fact: Set can be a noun, a verb, or an adjective.
fact: «Set» as a noun means a group of things that belong together, like a chess set.
fact: «Set» as a verb means to put something in a place, like «set the table».
fact: «Set» as an adjective means ready or fixed, like «a set time».
fact: In maths, a set is a collection of numbers or things: «a fraction like one third means: split the whole set into equal parts and take one part.»
exercise: «Set the cups on the table.» What does set mean here? | A group of things that belong together | * To put something in a place | The sun going down | Ready or fixed
exercise: «A loaf has a set number of slices, and a shop sells only whole loaves.» What does set mean here? | To put in a place | Firm, like jelly | A group of loaves | * Fixed or decided in advance
exercise: Maths: «Split the whole set into equal parts, then take one part.» In maths, what is a set? | * A collection of numbers or things | A place to put plates | A time at work | Jelly that has gone firm
test: «The story is set in a forest.» What does set mean here? | Firm, like jelly | A group of trees | Put in a box | * Takes place
test: «Inside the Arctic Circle, the Sun does not set in summer.» What does set mean here? | A group of suns | Become firm | * Go down below the horizon | Put on a table
exam: Which meaning of set fits «He will set the timer for five minutes»? | Firm, like jelly | * To make it ready for a time | A group of timers | The sun going down
